erage, color=NULL)</span></b><span lang=\"EN-CA\" style=\"color:black\"> # this command\r\n does not work.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-CA\" style=\"color:black\"> </span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-CA\" style=\"color:black\"> I get the following message:\r\n</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><b><span lang=\"EN-CA\" style=\"color:black\">“Error in warpRefMesh(&quot;specimen1PLY.ply&quot;, specimen1,  :\r\n</span></b></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><b><span lang=\"EN-CA\" style=\"color:black\">  File is not a mesh3d object or xyz matrix”</span></b></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-CA\" style=\"color:black\"> </span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"color:black\">For\r\n<b>average</b>, I followed the Geomorph guide and used the following:</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><b><span lang=\"EN-CA\" style=\"color:red\">average &lt;-mshape(Y$coords)\r\n</span></b><b><span lang=\"EN-CA\" style=\"color:black\"># ref</span></b></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><b><span lang=\"EN-CA\" style=\"color:red\">findMeanSpec(Y$coords)</span></b></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-CA\" style=\"color:black\"> </span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-CA\" style=\"color:black\">I think that my “mesh.coord&quot; and &quot;ref” are x, y, z matrices but maybe they are not and I’m missing something. Originally my data is a morphologika\r\n file so I saved the <b>specimen1</b> as a separate nts. file but maybe I didn’t formatted properly. Since it opens, I don’t understand where is the error.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"> </p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Just to make sure for the\r\n<span lang=\"EN-CA\" style=\"color:black\">“mesh.coord”, the data should be the raw data points for\r\n<b>specimen1 </b>but for the “ref”, they are the Procrustes coordinates for <b>specimen1</b>, is this correct?</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"> </p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-CA\" style=\"color:b